    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"massive success for the free-market ideology\" sounds a bit strong for an academic consensus. isn't it more of a debate? like, some people argue the growth wasn't even that significant compared to the damage done to the middle class. why would you call it a success rather than just a specific policy choice with massive trade-offs?",
